# Byte-exactness is the entire point of this repository, so git must never
# translate line endings on checkout.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (which defaults to core.autocrlf=true) rewrites
# every text file's LF to CRLF as it lands on disk. The files then hash
# differently from MANIFEST.sha256 and every single entry fails — on a clone that
# is otherwise perfectly intact. A Windows verifier's first command would report
# 221 failures and they would reasonably conclude the record was broken.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for every path: what is committed is
# what appears on disk, on every platform.
* -text
